From: Local build <local@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] EXP: input: send pointer motion to clients at most once per 750 us (KWIN_POINTER_MOTION_INTERVAL_US)

A mouse that reports at 4000-8000 Hz moved the pointer every 125-250 us, and ForwardInputFilter sent
every motion to the client under the pointer: wl_pointer.motion + frame, each one read, dispatched and
handled by the client's toolkit (hover, picking) while the screen shows one position per refresh. A
guest plasmashell spent 185 ms of CPU per second of 4000 Hz motion over its desktop (90 at 1000 Hz),
and a Qt-side merge could not remove the dispatch half (findings/qt-pointer-motion-2026-10-18.md).

Motions closer than KWIN_POINTER_MOTION_INTERVAL_US (default 750: a 1000 Hz mouse, about 1000 us apart with jitter, passes) to the last one sent are held by
PointerInterface (setMotionHeld); a precise timer sends the latest when the interval is over, and any
other event to the client (button, axis, enter, leave, warp) sends it first, so ordering is kept and a
click always follows the latest position. A 1000 Hz mouse is not affected. A locked or confined
pointer (games) gets every motion; relative pointer motion is never held. 0 restores the previous
behaviour; $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/kwin-pointer-motion-interval-us overrides the variable while it exists
(read at most once a second: an A/B in a running host session).

---

